## Install

```bash
uv sync --all-extras
```

## The command graph

Six commands form a DAG, not a fixed pipeline. Run `meds-model commands` to see which this model supports.

| Command | Reads | Writes |
|---|---|---|
| `preprocess_data` | an external MEDS dataset | `<data_dir>/patients/` |
| `preprocess_task` | a task file (ACES YAML or labels) | `<data_dir>/tasks/<name>/` |
| `pretrain` | patient data | a pretrained model directory |
| `infer` | patient data + a pretrained model | `<data_dir>/inference/<name>/` |
| `supervised_train` | patient data + a task (+ at most one prior artifact) | a supervised model directory |
| `predict` | patient data + a task + exactly one source | `predictions.parquet` |

`data_dir` is a shared workspace: `patients/` is written once and never modified, while `preprocess_task`
and `infer` append sibling subdirectories. Every artifact directory carries a `manifest.yaml` recording
what produced it and from which inputs, and is published atomically — so a directory that exists is a
directory that finished.

## Usage

```bash
{% if profile == 'supervised_basic' %}meds-model preprocess_data  external_meds_dir=$MEDS_ROOT output_data_dir=runs/data
meds-model preprocess_task  input_data_dir=runs/data external_task_file=$TASK
meds-model supervised_train input_data_dir=runs/data output_supervised_model_dir=runs/models/supervised
meds-model predict          input_data_dir=runs/data input_supervised_model_dir=runs/models/supervised \
                            output_predictions_dir=runs/predictions
{% elif profile == 'zero_shot_ar' %}meds-model preprocess_data external_meds_dir=$MEDS_ROOT output_data_dir=runs/data
meds-model pretrain        input_data_dir=runs/data output_pretrained_model_dir=runs/models/pretrained
meds-model preprocess_task input_data_dir=runs/data external_task_file=$ACES_YAML
meds-model infer           input_data_dir=runs/data input_pretrained_model_dir=runs/models/pretrained
meds-model predict         input_data_dir=runs/data input_pretrained_model_dir=runs/models/pretrained \
                           output_predictions_dir=runs/predictions
{% elif profile == 'every_query' %}meds-model preprocess_data external_meds_dir=$MEDS_ROOT output_data_dir=runs/data
meds-model pretrain        input_data_dir=runs/data output_pretrained_model_dir=runs/models/pretrained
meds-model preprocess_task input_data_dir=runs/data external_task_file=$ACES_YAML
meds-model predict         input_data_dir=runs/data input_pretrained_model_dir=runs/models/pretrained \
                           output_predictions_dir=runs/predictions
{% elif profile == 'motor_finetune' %}meds-model preprocess_data  external_meds_dir=$MEDS_ROOT output_data_dir=runs/data
meds-model pretrain         input_data_dir=runs/data output_pretrained_model_dir=runs/models/pretrained
meds-model preprocess_task  input_data_dir=runs/data external_task_file=$TASK
meds-model supervised_train input_data_dir=runs/data input_pretrained_model_dir=runs/models/pretrained \
                            output_supervised_model_dir=runs/models/supervised
meds-model predict          input_data_dir=runs/data input_supervised_model_dir=runs/models/supervised \
                            output_predictions_dir=runs/predictions
{% elif profile == 'probe' %}meds-model preprocess_data  external_meds_dir=$MEDS_ROOT output_data_dir=runs/data
meds-model pretrain         input_data_dir=runs/data output_pretrained_model_dir=runs/models/pretrained
meds-model preprocess_task  input_data_dir=runs/data external_task_file=$TASK
meds-model infer            input_data_dir=runs/data input_pretrained_model_dir=runs/models/pretrained
meds-model supervised_train input_data_dir=runs/data input_inference_subdir=inference/embeddings \
                            output_supervised_model_dir=runs/models/supervised
meds-model predict          input_data_dir=runs/data input_supervised_model_dir=runs/models/supervised \
                            output_predictions_dir=runs/predictions
{% else %}meds-model preprocess_data external_meds_dir=$MEDS_ROOT output_data_dir=runs/data
meds-model preprocess_task input_data_dir=runs/data external_task_file=$TASK
# ... then the commands listed by `meds-model commands`
{% endif %}```

Any extra argument is a Hydra override, e.g.
`meds-model supervised_train trainer.max_epochs=50 model.d_model=128`.

### Two rules worth knowing

**Sources are alternatives, not layers.** `supervised_train` and `predict` each accept several optional
input artifacts. Supplying more than one is an error rather than a precedence decision, and supplying one
the model does not handle is an error rather than a silently ignored argument.

**Predictions cover the whole index.** `predict` writes one row per task timepoint in the selected splits,
or fails. A short predictions file is indistinguishable downstream from a complete one, so it is never
written. Restrict the request with `splits=[held_out]` instead.

`predict` emits `predictions.parquet` in the
[meds-evaluation](https://github.com/kamilest/meds-evaluation) `PredictionSchema`
(`subject_id, prediction_time, predicted_boolean_probability`). **This repository ends at predicted
probabilities — it never reads ground-truth labels, and evaluation is a separate, shared tool.**

## Editing

- **`src/{{ model_slug }}/model.py`** — your `LightningModule`. Edit freely.
- **`src/{{ model_slug }}/commands.py`** — which commands this model supports.
- **`src/{{ model_slug }}/configs/`** — `model/` hyperparameters, `paths/` locations, `profile/` wiring.
- **`src/meds_model_base/`** — the vendored contract (managed by `copier update`; don't edit).

## Testing

```bash
uv run pytest -m "not slow"    # CLI + end-to-end pipeline smoke tests
uv run pytest -m slow          # synthetic-signal learnability property test
```

## Updating the template

```bash
copier update
```
